   "source": [
    "# AIR QUALITY ANALYTICS DASHBOARD\n",
    "### DSN2098 · Group 65 · Final Project Deliverable\n",
    "**Team:** Aryavardhan • Yugank Shakya • Akaksh Samdani • Anshu Sharma • Amrit Raj • Priyam Kumar\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. System Overview & Deliverable Functions\n",
    "This notebook integrates the complete end-to-end pipeline:\n",
    "1. **Current AQI Monitoring**: Latest reading panel from CPCB dataset\n",
    "2. **Future AQI Prediction**: XGBoost continuous regression & hazard spike classification\n",
    "3. **Area-wise Pollution Map**: Geospatial visualization of pollution levels\n",
    "4. **Pollution Alert**: Threshold-based rule engine (`prob_hazard >= 0.4`)\n",
    "5. **Pollution Trend Analysis**: STL decomposition (trend, seasonal, residual)\n",
    "6. **Weather & AQI Analysis**: Pollutant correlations & seasonal distributions\n",
    "7. **Pollution Source Analysis**: SHAP feature attribution"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import joblib\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "import shap\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set project root\n",
    "os.chdir('D:/projectexhibit-aiml')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load clean dataset & test splits\n",
    "clean_df = pd.read_csv('data/processed/clean_aqi.csv', parse_dates=['datetime'], index_col='datetime')\n",
    "test_df  = pd.read_csv('data/processed/test.csv', parse_dates=['datetime'], index_col='datetime')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load trained models\n",
    "xgb_reg = joblib.load('models/xgb_reg.pkl')\n",
    "xgb_clf, threshold = joblib.load('models/xgb_clf_hazard.pkl')\n",
    "\n",
    "target_cols = ['AQI', 'AQI_ord', 'hazard', 'AQI_Bucket']\n",
    "feature_cols = [c for c in test_df.columns if c not in target_cols]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Dashboard Loaded Successfully!\")\n",
    "print(f\"Clean Dataset Range: {clean_df.index.min().date()} to {clean_df.index.max().date()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Test Set Size: {len(test_df):,} rows\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Function 1: Current AQI Monitoring Panel"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "latest = clean_df.iloc[-1]\n",
    "print(\"=" * 45)\n",
    "print(f\" CURRENT AQI MONITORING PANEL ({clean_df.index[-1]})\")\n",
    "print(\"=" * 45)\n",
    "print(f\" AQI Value    : {latest['AQI']:.1f}\")\n",
    "print(f\" Category     : {latest['AQI_Bucket']}\")\n",
    "print(f\" PM2.5        : {latest['PM2.5']:.1f} µg/m³\")\n",
    "print(f\" PM10         : {latest['PM10']:.1f} µg/m³\")\n",
    "print(f\" NO2          : {latest['NO2']:.1f} µg/m³\")\n",
    "print(f\" SO2          : {latest['SO2']:.1f} µg/m³\")\n",
    "print(f\" CO           : {latest['CO']:.1f} mg/m³\")\n",
    "print(\"=" * 45)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Function 2 & 4: Future AQI Prediction & Pollution Alert Engine"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def predict_and_alert(sample_row):\n",
    "    X_sample = sample_row[feature_cols].to_frame().T\n",
    "    pred_aqi = xgb_reg.predict(X_sample)[0]\n",
    "    prob_hazard = xgb_clf.predict_proba(X_sample)[0][1]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    status = \"🚨 HAZARD ALERT (SEVERE SPIKE PREDICTED)\" if prob_hazard >= threshold else \"✅ NORMAL / MODERATE\"\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        \"Predicted_AQI\": round(pred_aqi, 2),\n",
    "        \"Hazard_Probability\": round(prob_hazard, 4),\n",
    "        \"Threshold\": threshold,\n",
    "        \"Alert_Status\": status\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "# Run prediction on latest test sample\n",
    "sample_eval = test_df.iloc[-1]\n",
    "res = predict_and_alert(sample_eval)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"FUTURE AQI PREDICTION & ALERT SYSTEM\")\n",
    "for k, v in res.items():\n",
    "    print(f\"  {k:<20} : {v}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Function 5: Pollution Trend Analysis (STL Decomposition)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from statsmodels.tsa.seasonal import STL\n",
    "\n",
    "stl_aqi = STL(clean_df['AQI'].ffill().bfill(), period=24, robust=True).fit()\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(4, 1, figsize=(14, 8), sharex=True)\n",
    "axes[0].plot(clean_df['AQI'], color='#4472c4', linewidth=0.5, label='Observed AQI')\n",
    "axes[0].set_title('Observed AQI Time Series', fontweight='bold')\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[1].plot(stl_aqi.trend, color='#ed7d31', linewidth=1.5, label='Trend')\n",
    "axes[1].set_title('STL Long-Term Trend', fontweight='bold')\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[2].plot(stl_aqi.seasonal, color='#70ad47', linewidth=0.5, label='Seasonal')\n",
    "axes[2].set_title('Daily Cyclical Seasonality (24h Period)', fontweight='bold')\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[3].plot(stl_aqi.resid, color='#a5a5a5', linewidth=0.5, label='Residual')\n",
    "axes[3].set_title('Residual Noise', fontweight='bold')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Function 6: Weather + AQI Correlation Heatmap"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "poll_cols = ['PM2.5', 'PM10', 'NO2', 'CO', 'SO2', 'O3', 'AQI']\n",
    "corr = clean_df[poll_cols].corr()\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(9, 6))\n",
    "sns.heatmap(corr, annot=True, cmap='RdBu_r', center=0, fmt='.2f', linewidths=0.5)\n",
    "plt.title('Pollutant Correlation Heatmap', fontweight='bold', fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Function 7: SHAP Feature Attribution"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "explainer = shap.TreeExplainer(xgb_reg)\n",
    "sample_test = test_df[feature_cols].sample(500, random_state=42)\n",
    "shap_values = explainer.shap_values(sample_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "shap.summary_plot(shap_values, sample_test, max_display=12)"
   ]
  }
 ],
